{"4876650":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"Never Sort By Color","steam_appid":4876650,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"controller_support":"full","detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><i>There is one rule of brick sorting. Everyone learns it the hard way.<\/i><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You've inherited a workshop and a Pile that swallowed it whole. <strong>Never Sort By Color<\/strong> is a zen organization sim about setting it right - sorting an impossibly huge mountain of plastic bricks into a perfectly labeled workshop, one satisfying handful at a time.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4876650\/extras\/7fdee751c430e6d0931f3d5b5f090d9b.poster.avif?t=1791299232\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4876650\/extras\/7fdee751c430e6d0931f3d5b5f090d9b.webm?t=1791299232\" type=\"video\/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4876650\/extras\/7fdee751c430e6d0931f3d5b5f090d9b.mp4?t=1791299232\" type=\"video\/mp4\"><\/video><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Tame the Pile<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Pile doesn't look conquerable. That's the point. Start by picking out bricks one at a time, and grow into an unstoppable sorting machine:<\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Magnet Glove<\/strong> - aim at a part and every loose copy rips out of the Pile and streams into your hand.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Sorter's Eye<\/strong> - mark a part type and watch every instance glow through the chaos.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Sieve Tray<\/strong> - scoop, shake, and let gravity sort a whole load by size in one motion.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Bucket Sort<\/strong> - bind bins to hotkeys and fling bricks blind over your shoulder, pure muscle memory.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Locators<\/strong> - hold up any brick and its home drawer lights up across the room.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Buy bins, trays, and cabinet walls. Stack them into towers. Label everything. Watch the floor appear.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Pull the parts. Watch it build.<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Instruction books lie scattered around the workshop, each one a MOC waiting for parts. Crack one open, pull its bill of materials from your perfect drawers, and watch the model <strong>build itself, brick by brick<\/strong> - a time-lapse of parts flying up and clicking into place, stud by stud.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is where your sorting pays off or bites. Honest drawers mean a full kit pulls in seconds. A contaminated drawer means the tray rejects your wrong part right in front of you.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Finished models don't ship away - they fill your workshop. A fire truck on the windowsill. A spaceship hung from the ceiling. Pick one up and swoosh it around the room. I won't tell.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Chaos in. Order out.<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One workshop, one enormous Pile, one deeply satisfying loop.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No timers, no fail states - just you, the bricks, and the quiet click of things going where they belong.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every brick you sort visibly shrinks the mountain. The before\/after is the game.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The Rule<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sorting by color feels right. It looks beautiful. And every brick collector on earth will tell you the same thing: you will never find anything again.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Sort by part. Always by part.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>Never. Sort. By. Color.<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p>","about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><i>There is one rule of brick sorting. Everyone learns it the hard way.<\/i><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You've inherited a workshop and a Pile that swallowed it whole. <strong>Never Sort By Color<\/strong> is a zen organization sim about setting it right - sorting an impossibly huge mountain of plastic bricks into a perfectly labeled workshop, one satisfying handful at a time.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4876650\/extras\/7fdee751c430e6d0931f3d5b5f090d9b.poster.avif?t=1791299232\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4876650\/extras\/7fdee751c430e6d0931f3d5b5f090d9b.webm?t=1791299232\" type=\"video\/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4876650\/extras\/7fdee751c430e6d0931f3d5b5f090d9b.mp4?t=1791299232\" type=\"video\/mp4\"><\/video><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Tame the Pile<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Pile doesn't look conquerable. That's the point. Start by picking out bricks one at a time, and grow into an unstoppable sorting machine:<\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Magnet Glove<\/strong> - aim at a part and every loose copy rips out of the Pile and streams into your hand.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Sorter's Eye<\/strong> - mark a part type and watch every instance glow through the chaos.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Sieve Tray<\/strong> - scoop, shake, and let gravity sort a whole load by size in one motion.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Bucket Sort<\/strong> - bind bins to hotkeys and fling bricks blind over your shoulder, pure muscle memory.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Locators<\/strong> - hold up any brick and its home drawer lights up across the room.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Buy bins, trays, and cabinet walls. Stack them into towers. Label everything. Watch the floor appear.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Pull the parts. Watch it build.<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Instruction books lie scattered around the workshop, each one a MOC waiting for parts. Crack one open, pull its bill of materials from your perfect drawers, and watch the model <strong>build itself, brick by brick<\/strong> - a time-lapse of parts flying up and clicking into place, stud by stud.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is where your sorting pays off or bites. Honest drawers mean a full kit pulls in seconds. A contaminated drawer means the tray rejects your wrong part right in front of you.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Finished models don't ship away - they fill your workshop. A fire truck on the windowsill. A spaceship hung from the ceiling. Pick one up and swoosh it around the room. I won't tell.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Chaos in. Order out.<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One workshop, one enormous Pile, one deeply satisfying loop.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No timers, no fail states - just you, the bricks, and the quiet click of things going where they belong.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every brick you sort visibly shrinks the mountain. The before\/after is the game.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The Rule<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sorting by color feels right. It looks beautiful. And every brick collector on earth will tell you the same thing: you will never find anything again.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Sort by part. Always by part.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>Never. Sort. By. Color.<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p>","short_description":"Somewhere under that mountain of bricks is your floor. Sort the impossible Pile with a magnet glove, sieves, and part-seeking vision. Fill labeled drawers, pull parts, watch MOC builds snap together brick by brick. Cozy, satisfying, and governed by one rule: never sort by color.","supported_languages":"English, French, Italian, German, Spanish - Spain, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese - Brazil, Russian, Simplified Chinese, Polish, Turkish, Traditional Chinese, Thai, Ukrainian, Vietnamese","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4876650\/482c3c99b58518d1dce87ebc9da82597aa8afd7b\/header.jpg?t=1791299232","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4876650\/45296ef3b6d1e6d19591f0a6a783b3f208d2c36a\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1791299232","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/4876650\/45296ef3b6d1e6d19591f0a6a783b3f208d2c36a\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1791299232","website":"https:\/\/legendstudio.com\/never-sort-by-color\/","pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 10 64-bit (version 21H2 or newer)<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Quad-core x64 with SSE4.2 (Intel Core i3-6100 \/ AMD Ryzen 3 1200)<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 8 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> DirectX 12-capable GPU with compute shader support, 2 GB VRAM (NVIDIA GeForce GTX 960 \/ AMD Radeon RX 460 \/ Intel UHD 620)<br><\/li><li><strong>DirectX:<\/strong> Version 12<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 1 GB available space<\/li><\/ul>"},"mac_requirements":[],"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Ubuntu 22.04 \/ SteamOS 3.0 or newer<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Quad-core x64 with SSE4.2 (Intel Core i3-6100 \/ AMD Ryzen 3 1200)<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 8 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Vulkan 1.1-capable GPU with compute shader support, 2 GB VRAM (NVIDIA GeForce GTX 960 \/ AMD Radeon RX 460 \/ Intel UHD 620); Mesa 22+ or NVIDIA 470+ drivers<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 1 GB available space<\/li><\/ul>"},"legal_notice":"Never Sort By Color is an independent game and is not affiliated with, sponsored by, authorized, or endorsed by the LEGO Group. LEGO® is a trademark of the LEGO Group of companies. The bricks in the game are generic plastic building bricks - but if you've ever sorted a real LEGO collection, you already know the rule."}}}